# Language: comments and commits

This repository is English-first.

- **Code comments** (including `//`, `/* */`, godoc, package docs): write in **English**. Do not add new Chinese comments; when touching nearby Chinese comments, prefer translating them to English in the same change.
- **Git commit messages**: write in **English** (imperative mood, short subject; optional body for why).

```go
// ❌ BAD
// 首次 Write 未调 WriteHeader 时补记 200

// ✅ GOOD
// Match net/http: first Write without WriteHeader implies status 200.
```

```text
❌ BAD: 修复 access log status 为 0
✅ GOOD: Record implicit HTTP 200 when Write runs without WriteHeader.
```

Chat with the user may still follow the consumer project's language (e.g. Chinese in rfv); this rule only covers in-repo comments and commits.
